{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi","id":1464762,"title":"So Ur-Shulgi...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-21T09:56:54-07:00","id":1464762,"title":"So Ur-Shulgi...","content":"... is still undead and well, despite some people claiming he and the path of blood practicioners had been wiped out.<br /> <br /> And the teachings of their cult seems in line with the original version of the assamites (including the &quot;protect mortals&quot; part!).<br /> <br /> Opinions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:05:58-07:00","id":1464764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi#post1464762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... is still undead and well, despite some people claiming he and the path of blood practicioners had been wiped out.<br /> <br /> And the teachings of their cult seems in line with the original version of the assamites (including the &quot;protect mortals&quot; part!).<br /> <br /> Opinions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, THE SABBAT says no one is sure because Alamut is a toxic magical radiation zone. It was also written after Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't be surprised if the Disciples of Ur-Shulgi are operating from old information.<br /> <br /> It's a shame that we didn't get their reaction to Alamut's loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:19:58-07:00","id":1464767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464764#post1464764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, THE SABBAT says no one is sure because Alamut is a toxic magical radiation zone. It was also written after Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't be surprised if the Disciples of Ur-Shulgi are operating from old information.<br /> <br /> It's a shame that we didn't get their reaction to Alamut's loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per the Sabbat IN CHARACTER piece, Alamut is not lost. It's out of reach for the followers of Al-Asharad. And the piece about the Sheperds clearly states that Ur-Shulgi left Alamut and is currently trying to increase his power (yeah...). For all we know Ur-Shulgi's servants may be able to come and go in and out of Alamut without problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:28:41-07:00","id":1464770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464767#post1464767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As per the Sabbat IN CHARACTER piece, Alamut is not lost. It's out of reach for the followers of Al-Asharad. And the piece about the Sheperds clearly states that Ur-Shulgi left Alamut and is currently trying to increase his power (yeah...). For all we know Ur-Shulgi's servants may be able to come and go in and out of Alamut without problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>He/It is reacting to the Beckoning nuking his/Its Disciplines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:37:42-07:00","id":1464773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464767#post1464767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As per the Sabbat IN CHARACTER piece, Alamut is not lost. It's out of reach for the followers of Al-Asharad. And the piece about the Sheperds clearly states that Ur-Shulgi left Alamut and is currently trying to increase his power (yeah...). For all we know Ur-Shulgi's servants may be able to come and go in and out of Alamut without problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ur-Shulgi isn't probably even in control of Alamut. The Three Eyed Salubri seemingly challenging him for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T13:05:45-07:00","id":1464788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464773#post1464773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ur-Shulgi isn't probably even in control of Alamut. The Three Eyed Salubri seemingly challenging him for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it is mentioned a &quot;three eyed witch&quot; may be in Alamut is basically heresay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He/It is reacting to the Beckoning nuking his/Its Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the least. He left Alamut after sending his disciples in the world with express orders to follow the Road of Blood and kill Ashirra and unbelievers (but mostly Ashirra), he claimed that he was doing so because he wanted to INCREASE his power.<br /> <br /> What I find interesting about this development is that the Sheperds background seems to ignore the development made in V20 about Ur-Shulgi (or rather, V20 made canon the origin that WW didn't want to publish back in the day, Ur-Shulgi as Shaitan). The Sheperds hunt other vampires especially &quot;traitor&quot; assamites but they also protect and treat humans fairly &quot;if possible&quot; (basically, the assamite creed before Revised). This is not consistent with Ur-Shulgi as an archinfernalist that cares not for Haqim's laws, quite the opposite actually.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T13:43:45-07:00","id":1464790,"title":"","content":"Something else about Ur Shulgi and Alamut. The <i>Sabbat </i>book tacitly suggests Alamut is in the Maghreb, or North Western Africa. Alamut is in the Middle East (the ruins of the real Alamut being in Iran). This is by grouping of the title of of the section, which otherwise does not mentioned the Maghreb. Eastern Libya is the closest, and that is still 3,500 miles from the region where the VtM Alamut is usually placed.<br /> <br /> Also, what if the three eyed witch is not a good Salubri gone to battle the Evil (tm) of Ur-Shulgi? What is the &quot;witch with three eyes&quot; is the Salubri-created Baali comes to possibly join with Ur-Shulgi, because nothing in the text specifies that the witch and Shulgi and fighting. We just assume that and project it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-21-2021, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T14:14:55-07:00","id":1464792,"title":"","content":"My theory on the three eyed witch. Its Tremere in Goatrixs Body looking to eat haqim before his magic ritual that makes him temp 3rd gen wares off lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:10:23-07:00","id":1464796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464790#post1464790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else about Ur Shulgi and Alamut. The <i>Sabbat </i>book tacitly suggests Alamut is in the Maghreb, or North Western Africa. Alamut is in the Middle East (the ruins of the real Alamut being in Iran). This is by grouping of the title of of the section, which otherwise does not mentioned the Maghreb. Eastern Libya is the closest, and that is still 3,500 miles from the region where the VtM Alamut is usually placed.<br /> <br /> Also, what if the three eyed witch is not a good Salubri gone to battle the Evil (tm) of Ur-Shulgi? What is the &quot;witch with three eyes&quot; is the Salubri-created Baali comes to possibly join with Ur-Shulgi, because nothing in the text specifies that the witch and Shulgi and fighting. We just assume that and project it.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Well keep in mind that in the WoD our Alamut is the false Alamut and its existence is adressed, and it was hinted that Alamut is actually a demon bastion so it has ways to be moved around or closed off if one knows what he's doing. That said I don't get the impression Alamut is in the Maghreb. The title is about Alamut AND the Maghreb which could imply the mountain fortress is still in Iran.<br /> <br /> 2. The problem with that story is that the in character author is reporting what the rafiqs told him. That Alamut is lost, that it's ruled by an ancient who's way older than the second generation (it's supposed to be Ur-Shulgi, but the bit about his age is hyperbole and makes it clear the author doesn't really know what he's talking about), that it's ruled by a witch with 3 eyes that entralls you with just a sip of her blood (seems like an ancient Salubri or Saulot), and that it's ruled by a sect of vampires that both reveres and fears the antediluvians (the True Black Hand?). The whole of this information is heresay, the Author of the piece has been outside Alamut and has seen portents of great magic but basically knows nothing for sure even when he reports events from the Maghreb and Egypt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:23:49-07:00","id":1464799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464788#post1464788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find interesting about this development is that the Sheperds background seems to ignore the development made in V20 about Ur-Shulgi (or rather, V20 made canon the origin that WW didn't want to publish back in the day, Ur-Shulgi as Shaitan). The Sheperds hunt other vampires especially &quot;traitor&quot; assamites but they also protect and treat humans fairly &quot;if possible&quot; (basically, the assamite creed before Revised). This is not consistent with Ur-Shulgi as an archinfernalist that cares not for Haqim's laws, quite the opposite actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Ur-Shulgi was claiming that everything he was doing for Haqim.<br /> <br /> Also, we know he follows the Path of Blood because we have Ur-Shulgi's stats. The thing was that Ur-Shulgi is a Baali or widdenslaite that just so happens to have been BRAINWASHED by Haqim. Basically, Haqim taking Damien Thorne the Antichrist and turning him into a hell-hunting servant.<br /> <br /> He might still be Baali but he's a Baali who is serving the cause of Haqim as he interprets it.<br /> <br /> You know, a being of arguable pure evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:47:23-07:00","id":1464802,"title":"","content":"Personally I always figured the little goblin was something possessing a methusulah rather than the methusulah itself.<br /> <br /> God only knows what it actually wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:49:29-07:00","id":1464803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464799#post1464799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean Ur-Shulgi was claiming that everything he was doing for Haqim.<br /> <br /> Also, we know he follows the Path of Blood because we have Ur-Shulgi's stats. The thing was that Ur-Shulgi is a Baali or widdenslaite that just so happens to have been BRAINWASHED by Haqim. Basically, Haqim taking Damien Thorne the Antichrist and turning him into a hell-hunting servant.<br /> <br /> He might still be Baali but he's a Baali who is serving the cause of Haqim as he interprets it.<br /> <br /> You know, a being of arguable pure evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the version of the story we are given in V20 (which is very similar to what the original author wanted but was scrapped in Assamite Revised) is that Ur-Shulgi WAS a widdenslaite that Haqim embraced using the same organ pit that spawned the 3 original Baali. Then Haqim used him to lure out the various Baali tribes so they could be smashed. Ur-Shulgi was at the head of the Baali until Haqim intervened and stopped him. The way Ur-Shulgi is presented in V20 resembles the way Shaitan was presented in Dark Ages Companion and actually solves one big problem with the Baali myths (which are a mess anyway so it's nice something got sorted out).<br /> <br /> That said, it's true that, later on, Ur-Shulgi became an effective killer of Baali, and he found a way to preserve one of the most effective demon hunters who ever existed, the archmage Al Asharad who became his childer (Haqim apparently wanted him dead because he killed &quot;Haqim favored childe&quot; in self defense, or so the story goes). Yet V20 basically makes clear that Ur-Shulgi doesn't care about Haqim at all. Now V5 presents the Sheperds and the Road of Blood in a more benignant way than you would expect from an archdiabolist bent of destroying the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T16:07:06-07:00","id":1464807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464803#post1464803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually the version of the story we are given in V20 (which is very similar to what the original author wanted but was scrapped in Assamite Revised) is that Ur-Shulgi WAS a widdenslaite that Haqim embraced using the same organ pit that spawned the 3 original Baali. Then Haqim used him to lure out the various Baali tribes so they could be smashed. Ur-Shulgi was at the head of the Baali until Haqim intervened and stopped him. The way Ur-Shulgi is presented in V20 resembles the way Shaitan was presented in Dark Ages Companion and actually solves one big problem with the Baali myths (which are a mess anyway so it's nice something got sorted out).<br /> <br /> That said, it's true that, later on, Ur-Shulgi became an effective killer of Baali, and he found a way to preserve one of the most effective demon hunters who ever existed, the archmage Al Asharad who became his childer (Haqim apparently wanted him dead because he killed &quot;Haqim favored childe&quot; in self defense, or so the story goes). Yet V20 basically makes clear that Ur-Shulgi doesn't care about Haqim at all. Now V5 presents the Sheperds and the Road of Blood in a more benignant way than you would expect from an archdiabolist bent of destroying the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the correction but I think you also miss a third take which is the fact the Disciples of Ur-Shulgi are a bunch of religious fanatics completely misreading their Dark Lord was always still going to do all of this in Haqim's name anyway.<br /> <br /> And murdering other Assamites (i.e. the people Haqim uses to protect the world) is still on the menu.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T18:49:18-07:00","id":1464812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464807#post1464807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the correction but I think you also miss a third take which is the fact the Disciples of Ur-Shulgi are a bunch of religious fanatics completely misreading their Dark Lord was always still going to do all of this in Haqim's name anyway.<br /> <br /> And murdering other Assamites (i.e. the people Haqim uses to protect the world) is still on the menu.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no doubt Haqim is not ok with most of his progeny, including Ur-Shulgi. In the Gehenna novel Haqim kills Teguryus (or was it Al-Asharad? Can't recall right now) because he disappointed him (this was after the Assamite split over Ur-Shulgi's actions and joined the Camarilla) but then Haqim met Fatima (who was a schismatic as well and he spared her after she refused to renounce her faith. So it's safe to say Haqim is not on the same page with Ur-Shulgi but he's probably not ok with what the schismatics have done either. He was said to have been fed up with his clan for a long time after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 10-21-2021, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T08:40:51-07:00","id":1464876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464799#post1464799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing was that Ur-Shulgi is a Baali or widdenslaite that just so happens to have been BRAINWASHED by Haqim. Basically, Haqim taking Damien Thorne the Antichrist and turning him into a hell-hunting servant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any clear evidence in lore or a writer's admission that Ur-Shulgi was/is a Widderslainte? Or is he just referred as a 'cursed child with a dark soul' or similar? If it is this then there are other options, it might happen in WoD that a person is born with particularly dark characteristics or grim destiny.<br /> <br /> This part is intriguing because considering how early during ancient history Ur-Shulgi lived, this would place the date of existence of the Widderslaintes - and thus, the Cauls (or some other initiation process for turning a Mage into a Barrabi and leads to the birth of a Widderslainte) - very early. While in MtA lore there are two contradictory pieces of information about this. In <i>Infernalism: Path of Screams</i> book it is given that the Nephandi formed during the medieval times, but in <i>Ascension </i>book the Nephandi victory scenario it is said that the Cauls / Inversion process was created around the time Christianity was established.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464812#post1464812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no doubt Haqim is not ok with most of his progeny</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder who from the Clan Founders is pleased and satisfied with his progeny? What does Arikel think about Clan Toreador? Do they get considered and judged based on the state of the art they support and the beauty they create? And what about the fact that they ended up being called Degenerates? Does Arikel approve? I think she does not, but who knows...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T03:25:13-07:00","id":1464986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464876#post1464876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any clear evidence in lore or a writer's admission that Ur-Shulgi was/is a Widderslainte? Or is he just referred as a 'cursed child with a dark soul' or similar? If it is this then there are other options, it might happen in WoD that a person is born with particularly dark characteristics or grim destiny.<br /> <br /> This part is intriguing because considering how early during ancient history Ur-Shulgi lived, this would place the date of existence of the Widderslaintes - and thus, the Cauls (or some other initiation process for turning a Mage into a Barrabi and leads to the birth of a Widderslainte) - very early. While in MtA lore there are two contradictory pieces of information about this. In <i>Infernalism: Path of Screams</i> book it is given that the Nephandi formed during the medieval times, but in <i>Ascension </i>book the Nephandi victory scenario it is said that the Cauls / Inversion process was created around the time Christianity was established.</div> </div> </div> </div>The material exists but was cut out of Assamite Revised. The idea was that some souls are destined for the Abyss no matter what. In a more general sense Ur-Shulgi was supposed to be some sort of &quot;antichrist&quot; figure, basically the Shaitan of Dark Ages Companion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder who from the Clan Founders is pleased and satisfied with his progeny? What does Arikel think about Clan Toreador? Do they get considered and judged based on the state of the art they support and the beauty they create? And what about the fact that they ended up being called Degenerates? Does Arikel approve? I think she does not, but who knows... </div> </div> </div>This depends on the clan: some hate their progeny (Nosferatu), some others (most?) simply do not care, they will use them as pawns and eat them all when the time comes, but a few might have a more complex relationship with their clan, in the case of Haqim it seems some (very few) of his progeny still have some value in his eyes and that goes beyond being useful pawns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T05:03:22-07:00","id":1464999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464986#post1464986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This depends on the clan: some hate their progeny (Nosferatu), some others (most?) simply do not care, they will use them as pawns and eat them all when the time comes, but a few might have a more complex relationship with their clan, in the case of Haqim it seems some (very few) of his progeny still have some value in his eyes and that goes beyond being useful pawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>This 'eat them all' part does sound like a scare or paranoia within the Kindred society, or some propaganda of Gehenna Cults. Did any Antediluvian ever do anything like this? I imagine it is more likely that, assuming an endgame, they have much much more complex and grand plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T08:29:17-07:00","id":1465012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464999#post1464999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This 'eat them all' part does sound like a scare or paranoia within the Kindred society, or some propaganda of Gehenna Cults. Did any Antediluvian ever do anything like this? I imagine it is more likely that, assuming an endgame, they have much much more complex and grand plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>At a certain point the Antediluvians might NEED to eat their progeny. It's what Ravnos had to do when he awakened he was low on blood and being attacked by 3 bodhisattavas so he called his progeny and started consuming it.<br /> <br /> The Gehenna book suggested a few different scenarios for this as well.<br /> <br /> As with everything else in the WoD it depends on what your views are about Gehenna, Caine, the Antediluvians and so on. I know how I did this but of course it's not like there's a definitive &quot;canonical&quot; answer, the WoD doesn't like giving those.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T02:45:47-07:00","id":1465112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465012#post1465012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At a certain point the Antediluvians might NEED to eat their progeny. It's what Ravnos had to do when he awakened he was low on blood and being attacked by 3 bodhisattavas so he called his progeny and started consuming it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I assume that Zapatasura was for some reason maddened or desperate during the Week of Nightmares, so this was not planned nor usual behavior of an Antediluvian. I do dislike the whole story, An Antediluvian basically behaving like a roving, destructive monster? I just cannot appreciate this idea at all. T</span>hough the whole event did serve a role in WoD back then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465012#post1465012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gehenna book suggested a few different scenarios for this as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I do recall some (most?) of the Antediluvians in the <i>Gehenna </i>book being very nasty and tyrannical. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">I find it very interesting that in the <i>Crucible of God</i> scenario, the Kindred manage to win the war against humanity after the Masquerade fails, reducing society to pre-industrial level. Who would think? And out of everyone, the Followers of Set are noted as being at the forefront, corrupting and taking out key mortals. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">And of course, there is this illustration of some of the Antediluvians gathered together (in the <i>Nightshade </i>scenario). It is especially noteworthy because it shows what Arikel looks like. It is nice that she just wears a simple robe, instead of some exquisite dress. Her being at the center and tilting her head slightly feels appropriate and significant. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">(The appearances of the other Clan Founders...well unfortunately they all seem to have, through either choice or circumstances, moved away from the beautiful human form. So I would say that them being shown in the illustration is not that notable.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-24-2021, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T04:35:16-07:00","id":1465118,"title":"","content":"I like Ur Shulgi.<br /> <br /> All he needs to do is defend The Mountain. Make it an unassailable bastion of reactionary craziness that continues to spread vicious assamite antagonists. And then we're good. Maybe once in a while he can show up to destroy a methuselah and plunge a city into chaos. He doesn't need to do more than that. Anything else is beneath him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T05:11:35-07:00","id":1465119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465012#post1465012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At a certain point the Antediluvians might NEED to eat their progeny. It's what Ravnos had to do when he awakened he was low on blood and being attacked by 3 bodhisattavas so he called his progeny and started consuming it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time of Thin Blood gave us a good, out of character explanation for that as well. One which, if we think about it, explains quite a bit about the Jyhad and Gehenna(s): Methuselahs Thirst isn't an either/or thing, it is a progressive condition. The Antediluvians are so old, it has progressed so far, only the fourth and fifth generation vitae can quench their thirst.<br /> <br /> So we can extrapolate that Antediluvians spend long periods in torpor, using their disciplines to make subtle moves in the Jyhad, punctuated by short periods of waking up, initially in a hunger frenzy, and then making moves in the physical world. Probably including seeding a crop of Fourth generations to reap next time they wake up. Then they sink back into torpor as the blood supply runs out. And their Jyhad priorities would include preserving their blood banks, sorry, childer and grandchider for the next round.<br /> <br /> And the Jyhad? Well the Thirst still progresses, and someday the Fifth and even Fourth will not satisfy. That will presumably be the last Gehenna, so they are on a clock.<br /> <br /> It is also notable that even in the depths of his frenzy, Ravnos did not eat any kindred but his own line. Tzimisce shows us that consuming other Antediluvians lineages is very risky indeed.<br /> <br /> We can speculate that Antediluvians that spent a lot of time active had some temporary workaround. Lasombra, frequent sirings and destruction of progeny that did not measure up, Haquim, ability to shatter the blood bond, Saulot, switching to a much younger body, etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T05:41:16-07:00","id":1465125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465118#post1465118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Ur Shulgi.<br /> <br /> All he needs to do is defend The Mountain. Make it an unassailable bastion of reactionary craziness that continues to spread vicious assamite antagonists. And then we're good. Maybe once in a while he can show up to destroy a methuselah and plunge a city into chaos. He doesn't need to do more than that. Anything else is beneath him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I never understood the negative sentiment towards him which sometimes appears on this forum. He is simply one of the more powerful and capable Kindred in the setting. In WoD there will inevitably be persons who can outmatch and overpower the vast majority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T05:50:02-07:00","id":1465127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465112#post1465112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And of course, there is this illustration of some of the Antediluvians gathered together (in the <i>Nightshade </i>scenario). It is especially noteworthy because it shows what Arikel looks like. It is nice that she just wears a simple robe, instead of some exquisite dress. Her being at the center and tilting her head slightly feels appropriate and significant.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Something tangential I've always wondered since first reading <i>Gehenna</i>: was &quot;Sarah the Shaper&quot; from the <i>Crucible of God</i> scenario originally intended to be Arikel?<br /> <br /> They match quite well\u2014the Shaping discipline parallels with potting, Arikel's original profession, her general humanity compared to the other Antediluvians (whether &quot;faked&quot; or not), her use of social wits to gain allies, Absimiliard's description of her (&quot;silly girl... throw pots at me... redocorate my haven&quot;).<br /> <br /> Major points against: she doesn't spam Presence, and one of her suggested targets is flat-out called &quot;Arikel, (founder of the Toreador).<br /> <br /> Anyway, to finish the tangent, I've always thought a good hook would have made the Shaper Arikel after some kind of major humbling (losing Presence?) and that she'd spent the time since getting back in touch with actual &quot;creation&quot; and developing Shaping; reigniting those original sparks of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26959-tofana-by-l-oreal","user":"Tofana by L'Oreal","date":". 10-24-2021, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26959-tofana-by-l-oreal","name":"Tofana by L'Oreal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T08:11:50-07:00","id":1465141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1464812#post1464812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no doubt Haqim is not ok with most of his progeny, including Ur-Shulgi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. The Antediluvians are somewhere between forces of nature (which cannot have morality, ethics or ideology) and sadistic psychopaths (who do not have morality, ethics or ideology). In as much as Haqim can even be understood in a rational manner, he is probably fine with Ur Shulgi trying to force the clan into worship of Haqim.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T08:13:13-07:00","id":1465142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465141#post1465141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree. The Antediluvians are somewhere between forces of nature (which cannot have morality, ethics or ideology) and sadistic psychopaths (who do not have morality, ethics or ideology). In as much as Haqim can even be understood in a rational manner, he is probably fine with Ur Shulgi trying to force the clan into worship of Haqim.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends if the Antediluvains have personalities or not in your view. Haqim's thing is he thinks he's doing the Tal'Mah'Ra thing of being humanity's protector while also being a horrible monster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T08:39:10-07:00","id":1465145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465142#post1465142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends if the Antediluvains have personalities or not in your view. Haqim's thing is he thinks he's doing the Tal'Mah'Ra thing of being humanity's protector while also being a horrible monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view of the Antediluvains is they have lost anything humane across 10,000 years owing to pain, hunger, malice, resentment and so on. Even then, to use a metaphor, farmers and ranchers will protect the sheep, cattle and pigs they own - protect them from thieves and wolves. But the ranchers and farmers still kill, butcher, skin and eat the pigs, cattle and sheep.<br /> <br /> The butcher cares not for the lamb's cry, they just don't to share the mutton. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T09:30:08-07:00","id":1465148,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a>, my personal problem with Ur-Shulgi is that it is a bland character with bland shows of power. Its power level and violence aren't problems by themselves, but I just don't feel like it improved the story.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a>, the Antediluvians can be like that, but they aren't necessarily like that. And likewise, you can interpret that being any of those things precludes morality, ethics and ideology, but this isn't necessarily true either. Psychopaths in particular are a real thing and, contrary to common belief, do have ethics and ideology, sometimes very strong ones (they don't have morality in a psychological sense, but it isn't quite like the common concept of morality).<br /> <br /> About the whole &quot;eating the childer&quot; shtick, it can be played in many ways. There are indicators in the setting that it works like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2471\" data-vbnamecard=\"2471\">Trollroot</a> said, but those could be strongly overestimated or outright lies, or even more complex than it seems.<br /> <br /> Not only that, not being morons it is likely that the Antediluvians are trying to avoid their ultimate fate, so it isn't unlikely that they have experiments in motion to outgrow their need for stronger blood and also to make themselves immune to becoming food. Some of them may have achieved it, completely sidestepping the Gehenna cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:32:58-07:00","id":1465160,"title":"","content":"My take on the Antediluvians is the Cyclical Gehenna is somewhat overexaggerated in terms of its destructiveness:<br /> <br /> 1. Antediluvian Embraces a bunch of childer.<br /> 2. Childer embrace a bunch of childer and they embrace and so on.<br /> 3. Antediluvian goes to sleep.<br /> 4. Antediluvian controls their childer from their torpor with Auspex and Dominate.<br /> 5. Antediluvian sleeps for 1000 years.<br /> 6. Antediluvian wakes up.<br /> 7. Antediluvian separates the &quot;Good&quot; vampires from the &quot;Bad&quot; vampires according to their alien morality.<br /> 8. Antediluvian eats all of the &quot;Bad&quot; Vampires.<br /> 9. Antediluvian gives their blood to or Embraces a bunch of new childer.<br /> 10. Repeat.<br /> <br /> Which means Gehenna happens all of the time but you don't hear about it as much as you might think because it's known primarily in the abstract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:39:50-07:00","id":1465163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465148#post1465148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, my personal problem with Ur-Shulgi is that it is a bland character with bland shows of power. Its power level and violence aren't problems by themselves, but I just don't feel like it improved the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately Ur-Shulgi suffers the same problem that the Fallen from D:tF do; the character was introduced to be a sign that Gehenna was really nigh. It didn't matter what his real motivation might have been, only that he was a danger and an escalation. It didn't matter that he was a gamebreaker, because the game was going to have an ending. He had one job, and it's done.<br /> <br /> It's only now that the game has to continue that he's this problem that has to be addressed. Like Kupala escaping at the end of Transylvania Chronicles, the Tremere plot to learn the entire human race's true name by sequencing the human genome, the thing lurking beneath Manhattan, and now Mary the Black forming a new Trinity with the soul of the diablerized Michael, there are some plot hints that are never really mean to come to full term. Whatever Ur-Shulgi's real agenda is, any counterforce that could plausibly thwart him reduces the players to the role of the human onlookers in a kaiju movie. It would be the Storyteller playing with his toys and making the players watch. <br /> <br /> Some plot elements are actually better dealt with offstage, I think. I wouldn't have minded if Ur-Shulgi's destruction had canonically come at the hands of the US Air Force or whoever in the plot dump that came with the launch of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:43:07-07:00","id":1465165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465163#post1465163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some plot elements are actually better dealt with offstage, I think. I wouldn't have minded if Ur-Shulgi's destruction had canonically come at the hands of the US Air Force or whoever in the plot dump that came with the launch of V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would have been hilarious and a better victory for the SI because unlike the Council of Seven, Ur-Shulgi doesn't know what a jet is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T11:10:54-07:00","id":1465167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465165#post1465165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would have been hilarious and a better victory for the SI because unlike the Council of Seven, Ur-Shulgi doesn't know what a jet is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree with that for so many reasons. But it is what it is.<br /> <br /> I did thought him a bad execution back then, contrary to DtF that I greatly enjoyed. The Week of Nightmares is an example of a thing that was ill conceived, full of problems, a mess hard to clean even today, but it was a lot of fun to read. I want to excise it from canon in the way it happened, but I can't say it made for a dull metaplot.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi just isn't the same. He came to bring changes that were needed, for sure. He had a power level that should have been expected to exist, maybe, I disagree but won't argue now. But he was simply dull. Instead of adding an interesting element he just made both the Tremere and the Assamite Sorcerers look like idiots. He lowered stakes instead of raising them. He's boring. Oh so boring.<br /> <br /> But as I said, it is what it is. The Onyx Plot God is alive and well, ready to make no difference whatsoever unless he decides to fart on a random plot again, with the subtlety of a Rules Lawyer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T11:17:44-07:00","id":1465169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465167#post1465167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally agree with that for so many reasons. But it is what it is.<br /> <br /> I did thought him a bad execution back then, contrary to DtF that I greatly enjoyed. The Week of Nightmares is an example of a thing that was ill conceived, full of problems, a mess hard to clean even today, but it was a lot of fun to read. I want to excise it from canon in the way it happened, but I can't say it made for a dull metaplot.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi just isn't the same. He came to bring changes that were needed, for sure. He had a power level that should have been expected to exist, maybe, I disagree but won't argue now. But he was simply dull. Instead of adding an interesting element he just made both the Tremere and the Assamite Sorcerers look like idiots. He lowered stakes instead of raising them. He's boring. Oh so boring.<br /> <br /> But as I said, it is what it is. The Onyx Plot God is alive and well, ready to make no difference whatsoever unless he decides to fart on a random plot again, with the subtlety of a Rules Lawyer.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thing is Ur-Shulgi is a jack you can let out of the box but you need to put it back at the end. Like, have the players release Kupala to kill him. THE FALL OF LONDON is a silly-silly adventure but if Mithras is at full power or dead is entirely on the players.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T12:28:35-07:00","id":1465174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465169#post1465169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My thing is Ur-Shulgi is a jack you can let out of the box but you need to put it back at the end. Like, have the players release Kupala to kill him. THE FALL OF LONDON is a silly-silly adventure but if Mithras is at full power or dead is entirely on the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, an RPG game should always be about player choices and agency. The party might not be able to take Ur-Shulgi (or Cthulhu or Acererak or whatever) in a one-on-one battle. But the choices o f the party should be the most important thing about the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T12:41:35-07:00","id":1465175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465174#post1465174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, an RPG game should always be about player choices and agency. The party might not be able to take Ur-Shulgi (or Cthulhu or Acererak or whatever) in a one-on-one battle. But the choices o f the party should be the most important thing about the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you of all people could figure out a good way to do a (if not cosmic) horror adventure game where the PCs get the ritual or do the thing to put Ur-Shulgi back to sleep or unmake him with his true name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T13:32:05-07:00","id":1465177,"title":"","content":"What is the generation of the Council of Seven and when does the attack on the Vienna Chantry happen in relation to Ur-Shulgi awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:12:13-07:00","id":1465189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465112#post1465112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I assume that Zapatasura was for some reason maddened or desperate during the Week of Nightmares, so this was not planned nor usual behavior of an Antediluvian. I do dislike the whole story, An Antediluvian basically behaving like a roving, destructive monster? I just cannot appreciate this idea at all. T</span>hough the whole event did serve a role in WoD back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right about the destruction of Ravnos having a role in the Revised era, but the event actually had an explanation: the Kuei-jin attacked the indian Ravnos (the dominant cainites of the region) killing a lot of them. The bloodshed caused Ravnos to awaken... hungry and maddened. He was then attacked by the Bodhisattavas and had to call his progeny to feed (which he did to an extent) even so it took an awful lot (the Technocracy going full Ragnarock protocol) to end him. Btw Ravnos being DEAD is one of the few canoncial facts about the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">I do recall some (most?) of the Antediluvians in the <i>Gehenna </i>book being very nasty and tyrannical. </span> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, their personalities (and identities) change from scenario to scenario though. This makes clear there's no definitive canonical depiction of who or what the Antediluvians are. In regards to Haqim, in one of the scenarios he refuses to join the other Antediluvians, gathers his clan in Alamut and plans to attack the others (led by Set IIRC). He was not online with their world dominating plans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">I find it very interesting that in the <i>Crucible of God</i> scenario, the Kindred manage to win the war against humanity after the Masquerade fails, reducing society to pre-industrial level. Who would think? And out of everyone, the Followers of Set are noted as being at the forefront, corrupting and taking out key mortals. </span> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering how the Foolowers of Set are them corrupting and enslaving mortals is nothing unexpected...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">And of course, there is this illustration of some of the Antediluvians gathered together (in the <i>Nightshade </i>scenario). It is especially noteworthy because it shows what Arikel looks like. It is nice that she just wears a simple robe, instead of some exquisite dress. Her being at the center and tilting her head slightly feels appropriate and significant. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">(The appearances of the other Clan Founders...well unfortunately they all seem to have, through either choice or circumstances, moved away from the beautiful human form. So I would say that them being shown in the illustration is not that notable.)</span> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't put much stock in those illustrations, those are samples of how the Antediluvians MIGHT look, it's nothing definitive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:18:50-07:00","id":1465190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465177#post1465177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the generation of the Council of Seven and when does the attack on the Vienna Chantry happen in relation to Ur-Shulgi awakening?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Members of the Co7 were all 4th generation (serial diablerie back in the day). Their personal power varied though.<br /> 2. The timetable isn't clear (as far as I know at least) but going by BJD, Ur-Shulgi awoke several years prior the destruction of the prime chantry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 10-24-2021, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:27:55-07:00","id":1465194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465177#post1465177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the generation of the Council of Seven and when does the attack on the Vienna Chantry happen in relation to Ur-Shulgi awakening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does it matter? To answer the first, by the way, 4th. They're all 4th gen through diablerie, even the young ones, and the older ones had centuries as powerful Mages before turning into vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:35:55-07:00","id":1465196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465119#post1465119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time of Thin Blood gave us a good, out of character explanation for that as well. One which, if we think about it, explains quite a bit about the Jyhad and Gehenna(s): Methuselahs Thirst isn't an either/or thing, it is a progressive condition. The Antediluvians are so old, it has progressed so far, only the fourth and fifth generation vitae can quench their thirst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and this concept was translated in V5 as well. Also keep in mind, Gehenna had &quot;the Withering&quot;, the thinning of the blood with all vampires becoming progressively weaker unless they diablerized their kind. This affected even antediluvians and is directly related to Theo Bell kinng Hardestadt in the Gehenna novel. V5 kept much of what was in the End Times line without bringing Gehenna to its catastrphic conclusion. So we don't have the withering but we have the beckoning, Theo Bell killed Hardestadt, the Vienna chantry falling and so on. All that stuff happened in the Gehenna novel. In V5 Gehenna happened but it wasn't the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So we can extrapolate that Antediluvians spend long periods in torpor, using their disciplines to make subtle moves in the Jyhad, punctuated by short periods of waking up, initially in a hunger frenzy, and then making moves in the physical world. Probably including seeding a crop of Fourth generations to reap next time they wake up. Then they sink back into torpor as the blood supply runs out. And their Jyhad priorities would include preserving their blood banks, sorry, childer and grandchider for the next round. </div> </div> </div>The Antediluivans descriptions and motives were left deliberately vague. They might be immortal chessmasters. They might be unreasoning forces of nature. They might be inhuman and utterly alien blood gods. There's no clear answer, you, as the ST get to decide. Personally I'm partial to making each one of them different from the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Jyhad? Well the Thirst still progresses, and someday the Fifth and even Fourth will not satisfy. That will presumably be the last Gehenna, so they are on a clock.<br /> <br /> It is also notable that even in the depths of his frenzy, Ravnos did not eat any kindred but his own line. Tzimisce shows us that consuming other Antediluvians lineages is very risky indeed.<br /> <br /> We can speculate that Antediluvians that spent a lot of time active had some temporary workaround. Lasombra, frequent sirings and destruction of progeny that did not measure up, Haquim, ability to shatter the blood bond, Saulot, switching to a much younger body, etc. </div> </div> </div>Personally I like the idea that Antediluvian power waxes and wanes, which means they are not always godlike... but they are still extremely powerful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:51:28-07:00","id":1465199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465141#post1465141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree. The Antediluvians are somewhere between forces of nature (which cannot have morality, ethics or ideology) and sadistic psychopaths (who do not have morality, ethics or ideology). In as much as Haqim can even be understood in a rational manner, he is probably fine with Ur Shulgi trying to force the clan into worship of Haqim.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a way to portray them. But from the little we know about them this is mostly not the case. The way Haqim was portrayed in the Gehenna novel is a windstorm who judges his progeny. Some are found wanting and are destroyed but others are spared and this fits his role as the judge of cainites. It also fits the facts about him listed in the revised clanbook and in Libellus Sanguinis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:35:18-07:00","id":1465207,"title":"","content":"I feel the lack of the Withering was a big mistake as it could have explained why all stats are limited to 5s now. You can just say the non-Beckoned Elders are losing their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:58:55-07:00","id":1465211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465194#post1465194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it matter? To answer the first, by the way, 4th. They're all 4th gen through diablerie, even the young ones, and the older ones had centuries as powerful Mages before turning into vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ask because I had an amusing thought of Ur-Shulgi being behind the attack on the Vienna Chantry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:29:28-07:00","id":1465216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465211#post1465211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask because I had an amusing thought of Ur-Shulgi being behind the attack on the Vienna Chantry.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the spanish inquisition. No one expected it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:32:46-07:00","id":1465218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465207#post1465207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the lack of the Withering was a big mistake as it could have explained why all stats are limited to 5s now. You can just say the non-Beckoned Elders are losing their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I detest the Beckoning, but as clumsy as it is the withering would have been a thousand times more impactful on the game. At least the Beckoning you can ignore, if all vampires (ALL, including thin bloods and antediluvians) start losing their blood powers and need diablerie to retain them the setting becomes a clusterfuck in no time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:33:49-07:00","id":1465219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465218#post1465218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I detest the Beckoning, but as clumsy as it is the withering would have been a thousand times more impactful on the game. At least the Beckoning you can ignore, if all vampires (ALL, including thin bloods and antediluvians) start losing their blood powers and need diablerie to retain them the setting becomes a clusterfuck in no time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not what I said and I deliberately said it should be an in-universe explanation for the rules changes that have already been implemented.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:37:32-07:00","id":1465221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465219#post1465219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's not what I said and I deliberately said it should be an in-universe explanation for the rules changes that have already been implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... the Withering had mechanical rules (they were brutal) and &quot;in setting&quot; there never was anything like 7th and lower generation vampires losing their elder disciplines. Those are now conflated into the 5 dot powers and combo disciplines.<br /> <br /> Edit: to further clarify, there's no need for an in universe explanation because the elder powers didn't stop existing, the mechanics changed and that's all. The same is true for stats. An elder can still use the power of his blood to achieve more than a human or a lesser vampire can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 10-24-2021, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T18:04:42-07:00","id":1465225,"title":"","content":"Although it may not be needed, there could be such explanation. And not only would that alleviate it for players that feel the need for such explanation, that would also incorporate a canonical lore, as the Withering IS canonical despite your scenario.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> didn't said to assume the Withering as still in effect, either. A week of that dread stuff could do the trick.<br /> <br /> Personally, while CTPhipps likes V5 because it changed the setting, one of my main criticisms is that it was too shy to change it enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T19:12:24-07:00","id":1465232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi#post1464762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... is still undead and well, despite some people claiming he and the path of blood practicioners had been wiped out.<br /> <br /> And the teachings of their cult seems in line with the original version of the assamites (including the &quot;protect mortals&quot; part!).<br /> <br /> Opinions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, back on topic.<br /> <br /> 1. Ur Shulgi is going to stay undead because vampires usually stay vampires. They usually don't stop being undead until they are forced into final death.<br /> <br /> 2. I don't think all the blood magicians of the Banu Haqim died. Most of them joined the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 3. It's debatable how much Ur Shulgi's cult closely matches the teaching of Haqim, given that all of it seems to be all over the place.<br /> <br /> My thoughts of Ur Shulgi are the same as those on the other 4th generation vampire, 3rd generation vampires and for that matter the Chosen in the Forgotten Realms; they only matter if the PCs encounter them for some reason. And even if the PC encounter them, the game should be about the PCs and not these nearly untouchable NPCs. A campaign sending the coterie anywhere near Alamut is not in the top five kinds of campaigns I would run.<br /> <br /> That said, he is a bit of a Cthulhu figure; a figure of terrible power and terrible age and his rising will be part of what ends the world. While the PCs cannot fight him, they can deal with the local chapter of his cult.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T19:28:51-07:00","id":1465233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465221#post1465221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... the Withering had mechanical rules (they were brutal) and &amp;quot;in setting&amp;quot; there never was anything like 7th and lower generation vampires losing their elder disciplines. Those are now conflated into the 5 dot powers and combo disciplines.<br /> <br /> Edit: to further clarify, there's no need for an in universe explanation because the elder powers didn't stop existing, the mechanics changed and that's all. The same is true for stats. An elder can still use the power of his blood to achieve more than a human or a lesser vampire can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that can't be true, 9 levels of Quietus and Assamite Sorcery doesn't track onto 5 Blood Sorcery powers, their are things he could do that he no longer can (and that's before Celerity getting made a waste of xp is mentioned) there is a massive difference in ability between a V20 Methuselah and a V5 one, the irony being they are now supposed to be blood gods when they are now able to be killed by semi competent coteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T07:52:21-07:00","id":1465278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465233#post1465233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that can't be true, 9 levels of Quietus and Assamite Sorcery doesn't track onto 5 Blood Sorcery powers, their are things he could do that he no longer can (and that's before Celerity getting made a waste of xp is mentioned) there is a massive difference in ability between a V20 Methuselah and a V5 one, the irony being they are now supposed to be blood gods when they are now able to be killed by semi competent coteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 has an open system you can invent, add and adapt old 6+ discipline powers and give them to elders easily enough. There is a mechanical problem and that is the fact in V5 all vampires have a max of 5 powers per discipline. That is something that needs to change imo, but it's not like this limit is hard coded in the lore of V5. The lore says elders are more powerful than neonates, and IN THE CONTEXT OF THE EDITION this is actually true. If you don't want to house rule the limit into oblivion (which I suggest you do) you can still give them 5 &quot;elder powers&quot; per discipline, in terms of lore nothing changes.<br /> As for celerity, of course the old celerity was more powerful than the current one. From day one it was a super powerful discipline that caused games to stall making some turns 5 minutes long. It was terribly designed and executed and a staple of powergamers everywhere, adding a rocket-tag element to vampire the game didn't need (so... the Methuselah goes first, he's got 8 dots in celerity, 8 dots in potence and deals aggravated damage... here's how you die). The current celerity and all other diciplines should be judged in the context of the current edition and considering what you might face they are mostly fine as they do their job. I.E. stuff like &quot;Blink&quot; is pretty damn powerful in V5 even if it wouldn't be in V1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T08:22:20-07:00","id":1465280,"title":"","content":"RAW, not at all. <br /> <br /> Ur Shulgi as a several thousand year old methuselah isn't going to be much different from your standard fare 300 year old elder, especially as he just woke from a long Torpor. He may heal faster and have some horrendous feeding issues, but there's not more to that. Very much killable by a PC party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T08:30:49-07:00","id":1465281,"title":"","content":"A &quot;problem&quot; being easy to solve isn't the same as it not existing, and easy houserule is still houserule. While we have no canonical affirmation in this regard, for official mechanics we do had the disappearance of elder powers and high level Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Will the game make an official statement on this? I don't know. Can they include rules for elder powers in future supplements? Yes. But they can also decide this isn't a thing anymore and roll with it. You can't say. If they decide so, then using the Withering as an explanation is an option, better than retconing those powers out of lore, which they can also do if they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T09:33:00-07:00","id":1465287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465225#post1465225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it may not be needed, there could be such explanation. And not only would that alleviate it for players that feel the need for such explanation, that would also incorporate a canonical lore, as the Withering IS canonical despite your scenario.<br /> <br /> [USER=&amp;quot;12002&amp;quot;]<br /> <br /> Personally, while CTPhipps likes V5 because it changed the setting, one of my main criticisms is that it was too shy to change it enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree, them wanting to have a cake and eat it too is the biggest issue in WOD v5. Instead of a completely modern take on World of Darkness or a love letter to the old one we have a misshapen amalgam that angers the old guard with needless or poorly concieved changes and confuses new players with archaic system and references to 10+ years of published material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T09:59:03-07:00","id":1465289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465287#post1465287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to agree, them wanting to have a cake and eat it too is the biggest issue in WOD v5. Instead of a completely modern take on World of Darkness or a love letter to the old one we have a misshapen amalgam that angers the old guard with needless or poorly concieved changes and confuses new players with archaic system and references to 10+ years of published material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that this falls apart under the point that the reason there's a 5th Edition is because Requiem never achieved anywhere near the popularity of V:TM or....well, 5th Edition. Mind you, it keeps coming back to the fact that as much as some elements seem to drive fans crazy, 5th Edition is a smashing enormous success.<br /> <br /> Sort of like Star Trek: Discovery. You may not like everything but it's something that has made an enormous impact and revived the franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T11:51:36-07:00","id":1465299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465289#post1465289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that this falls apart under the point that the reason there's a 5th Edition is because Requiem never achieved anywhere near the popularity of V:TM or....well, 5th Edition. Mind you, it keeps coming back to the fact that as much as some elements seem to drive fans crazy, 5th Edition is a smashing enormous success.<br /> <br /> Sort of like Star Trek: Discovery. You may not like everything but it's something that has made an enormous impact and revived the franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least for me, it is not about making a new setting. It is about driving the setting to its logical conclusion without holding up. They held up a lot.<br /> <br /> Metaplot-wise, the whole point of V5 is that the Gehenna came. Revised ended with the literal End of Times. The Old World is dead. Whatever we have now is what raised from its ashes. Several themes were affected by the Millennial tone of the game, that we're living in the End of History and nearing its culmination.<br /> <br /> Do you want to advance the clock but keep the themes untouched? V20 existed for that. Follow through it instead of weakening it. Work on a V28 or something and make the bolder updates without pushing the envelope too much.<br /> <br /> But to go ahead and say &quot;this isn't a Legacy Edition, this is the World Continuing&quot;, then you can't be shy of throwing old themes through the window.<br /> <br /> Create a Gehenna Scenario and run through its conclusion. Have the world really upside down. Break the Masquerade with a sledgehammer. Put Antes walking in the open. Have scars of the End Times and theories about the Red Star. Divorce the setting from the real world going full Alternate History. This is not Kansas anymore.<br /> <br /> They didn't do that, and that is my biggest complaint, something I won't withdraw lightly. Is it deal breaker? Nope. As I said before, when everything was said and done, the only deal breaker for me was NuCam, everything else is passable. Badly written, but acceptable concepts. But at the core, it is the shyness from making it properly post-Gehenna what I identify as the root cause of most of the bad writing and what makes V5 fall short of its potential. It is what makes me simply see V20 as better lore-wise and don't consider V5 lore as worth my time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:06:29-07:00","id":1465301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464762-so-ur-shulgi?p=1465289#post1465289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of like Star Trek: Discovery. You may not like everything but it's something that has made an enormous impact and revived the franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coming soon, <i>VtM Lower Decks. </i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:13:59-07:00","id":1465302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gra